==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|unþio-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|unt-|lang=ang}}.  Germanic cognates include Old Saxon [[uðia|ūðia]], Old High German [[undea]], Old Norse [[unnr]], [[uðr]].  The IE root is also the source of Latin [[unda]].

